error[endless_recursion]: every path through `bytes` calls `bytes` again before it returns, so no call to it can return
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-457-an-endless-recursion-is-told-its-ways-out.hero:9:12
    |
  9 |     return s.bytes()  #~ endless_recursion
    |            ^^^^^^^^^
  note: `s.bytes()` calls `bytes` with `s` first, since `x.f(y)` is `f(x, y)`, and inside `function bytes` that is this function
  note: a call to `bytes` gives nothing back until the call it makes does, and that one makes another: give `bytes` a path that returns before the call, or ends on `exit(code:)`, `assert false` or a `while true` with no `break` of its own; an overflow or an index out of bounds stops the program and is no such path

